>> title: Red Bean Ice
>> category: Drinks
>> tags: adzuki, evaporated milk, hong kong, iced, drink
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: red bean ice, 紅豆冰, hung dau bing, hong dau bing, iced red bean, red bean drink, adzuki ice, hong kong red bean ice, red bean with ice
>> pairs-with: red-bean-paste
>> servings: 4
>> time: 3 hr 15 min
>> slack: narrow — twenty minutes more and the beans go to paste, which is a different recipe on this shelf

>> step: boil 5 min, drain the first water
Cover @dried adzuki beans{1%cup}(200 g) with @water for the first boil{6%cup}(1.4 L) in a #saucepan{}, bring to a ~boil{5%min}, then drain.

>> step: simmer 60 min, whole not mashed
Return @&(~1)beans{} to the pan with @fresh water{4%cup}(950 mL) and ~simmer{60%min}, topping up so they stay covered, until a bean gives to a spoon and still holds its skin.

>> step: simmer with the sugar 10 min, chill 2 hr
Stir @rock sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g) into @&(~1)beans{} and ~simmer{10%min} to a loose syrup, then ~chill{2%hr}.

>> step: spoon the beans over the ice, milk down the side
Spoon @&(~1)sweet beans{} over @crushed ice{2%cup} in tall #glasses{} and pour @evaporated milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) down the side.
